@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Lessons & Help"; }
<header class="help-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Lessons &amp; Help</p><h1>Make your story, one clear step at a time.</h1><p>My Africa, My Narrative helps you turn your own recordings, words and images into a short private documentary while keeping you in control of every source.</p></div><nav class="lesson-jumps" aria-label="Help topics"><a href="#before">Before you begin</a><a href="#record">1. Record</a><a href="#shape">2. Shape</a><a href="#make">3. Make</a><a href="#export">4. Export</a></nav></header>

<section id="before" class="surface help-section"><p class="eyebrow">Before you begin</p><h2>What you need</h2><div class="requirement-grid"><article><span aria-hidden="true">🎙</span><h3>Your voice</h3><p>A recording made in the app or a permitted MP3, WAV, M4A, WebM or WebA file.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">▣</span><h3>A real visual</h3><p>At least one permitted photo or video that belongs with the story.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><h3>Permission</h3><p>Confirm honestly that you may use each source. Owner attestation is not independent verification.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">◷</span><h3>A little time</h3><p>A preview may be any length. A final documentary must last 60–90 seconds, including the 5-second credits card.</p></article></div><div class="notice"><strong>Privacy:</strong> Sources are stored privately and are available only through authorised routes. Do not upload material you do not have permission to use.</div></section>

<section class="lesson-grid">
<article id="record" class="surface lesson-card"><div class="lesson-number">1</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Record</p><h2>Collect original sources</h2><ol><li>Create or open a project.</li><li>Record with your microphone, or upload an existing audio file.</li><li>Or record a video — sound and picture together, up to two minutes. Hold your phone upright; films are vertical.</li><li>Stop and review the recording.</li><li>Confirm permission and save it to Sources.</li><li>Add at least one photo or video for the picture.</li></ol><p class="lesson-result"><strong>Ready to continue when:</strong> Sources shows permitted audio and a permitted image or video.</p></div></article>
<article id="shape" class="surface lesson-card"><div class="lesson-number">2</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Shape</p><h2>Choose the words and scenes</h2><ol><li>Listen to your source recording.</li><li>Mark where the words start and end, then type exactly what was said.</li><li>Save the reviewed transcript.</li><li>Create scenes using original audio, a real visual and caption text. Words marked “From your recording” must match the reviewed transcript and sit inside its range.</li><li>Optionally add a translated caption in your second language; it stays a draft until a fluent review is recorded.</li><li>Edit, remove or reorder scenes, review the cut and approve the exact revision.</li><li>Record a fluent language review of that exact revision.</li></ol><p><strong>Timing tip:</strong> play the recording and press “Set start from player” when the words begin and “Set end from player” when they end. You can also type seconds, such as <code>5</code> and <code>18.5</code>, then press “Play this stretch” to check.</p><p class="lesson-result"><strong>Ready to continue when:</strong> the current revision contains scenes and is approved.</p></div></article>
<article id="make" class="surface lesson-card"><div class="lesson-number">3</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Make</p><h2>Plan with what is real</h2><ol><li>Add the equipment, people, locations, time and optional budget you actually have.</li><li>Describe availability or limits.</li><li>Mark a resource unavailable when circumstances change.</li><li>Build a shot list: add your own shots, or ask for one suggested shot per scene using only available resources.</li><li>Mark each shot captured with the uploaded footage, or drop it. Planned shots count as missing footage and block the final export.</li><li>If a resource becomes unavailable, its shots are flagged so you can replan with what remains.</li></ol><p class="lesson-result"><strong>Important:</strong> the app never invents people, locations, equipment, prices or footage.</p></div></article>
<article id="export" class="surface lesson-card"><div class="lesson-number">4</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Export</p><h2>Preview, review and finish</h2><ol><li>Add credits for the storyteller, contributors and sources, then approve those exact credits.</li><li>Resolve every readiness message.</li><li>Queue a preview to test picture, original voice and captions.</li><li>Refresh while the durable Worker processes the job.</li><li>Open the PreviewVideo and Captions under Current artifacts.</li><li>For a 60–90 second approved cut, queue the 1080 × 1920 final.</li></ol><p><strong>Job meanings:</strong> Queued is waiting; Running is rendering; Succeeded has files; Failed shows an actionable reason.</p><p class="lesson-result"><strong>Artifacts:</strong> the MP4 film has your captions and an end credits card burned in. The SRT files hold the same captions (and translations, if written). They are tied to the exact approved revision and credits.</p></div></article>
</section>

<section class="surface help-section"><p class="eyebrow">Quick answers</p><h2>Common questions</h2><details><summary>Why can’t I add a scene?</summary><p>A scene requires permitted audio, a permitted image/video and a valid range where the end is after the start and stays within the recording.</p></details><details><summary>Why can I preview but not export the final?</summary><p>The final needs a fluent language review of the current revision, approved credits, no planned shots still missing, captions that keep your protected expressions, and 60–90 seconds including the credits card. The Export checklist names whatever is still outstanding.</p></details><details><summary>Why was my quoted scene refused?</summary><p>Words marked “From your recording” must link to a reviewed transcript of the same audio, stay inside its timing, and repeat its words. Correct the transcript first, or mark the wording as written by you.</p></details><details><summary>What happens after I change a scene?</summary><p>The change creates a new immutable revision. Review and approve that new revision, then render it again.</p></details><details><summary>Does the app replace my voice?</summary><p>No. Export trims and uses your selected original recording. Corrected caption text remains separate from the recorded speech.</p></details></section>

